# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase Admin — server side only, used ONLY when saving/loading flows.
# Firestore Database > create in test mode, then Project settings >
# Service accounts > Generate new private key.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=
# Keep the surrounding quotes and the literal \n escapes from the JSON key file.
FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END PRIVATE KEY-----\n"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Firebase Auth — OPTIONAL, and all-or-nothing.
#
# Leave these blank and the dashboard runs unauthenticated: no sign-in screen,
# flows shared by everyone who can reach the server. That is the right default
# for a tool running on localhost, and it is what keeps `npm run e2e` working.
#
# Fill ALL THREE in and sign-in becomes required, with each recording owned by
# the account that saved it. The same three values gate the server, so a token
# is verified whenever the client is expected to send one.
#
# Where: Firebase console > Project settings > General > Your apps > Web app.
# Then: Authentication > Sign-in method > enable Google and/or Email/Password,
# and add your domain (localhost is there by default) under Authorised domains.
#
# These are PUBLIC by design — they identify the project, they do not grant
# access. Firestore rules and the server's token check are what protect data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
